From: Betterr <51264180+Star-caorui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:44:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BatteryStatsImpl: Use Wi-Fi radio active time when the
 controller has no stats

Without enhanced power reporting (no link layer stats from the driver),
WifiPowerStatsProcessor estimates Wi-Fi power as active time times
wifi.active, plus scans. WifiPowerStatsCollector takes that active time
from getWifiActiveDuration(), which returns the global "Wi-Fi running"
time. Nothing reports Wi-Fi running any more: BatteryStatsManager has no
API for it and noteWifiRunning() has no callers, so that timer stays at
zero and Wi-Fi is charged nothing on these devices.

The Wi-Fi radio active timer is what tracks data activity: the network
stack moves it from the interface idle timer through
noteWifiRadioPowerState(). Use it instead. The power is then shared
between apps by their packets, as before.

On a Redmi Note 13 5G (MediaTek MT6833, no link layer stats in its
firmware), after about five hours on battery: Wi-Fi running 0 ms, Wi-Fi
radio active 4 h 14 min, and no Wi-Fi entry in the battery usage.

Change-Id: If4dabd297a1c7bf7409cec53792c7dc224195dd2
---
 .../java/com/android/server/power/stats/BatteryStatsImpl.java   | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/stats/BatteryStatsImpl.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/stats/BatteryStatsImpl.java
index 73e4d7c3..af91dcbb 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/stats/BatteryStatsImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/stats/BatteryStatsImpl.java
@@ -373,7 +373,7 @@ public class BatteryStatsImpl extends BatteryStats {
                 @Override
                 public long getWifiActiveDuration() {
                     synchronized (BatteryStatsImpl.this) {
-                        return getGlobalWifiRunningTime(mClock.elapsedRealtime() * 1000,
+                        return getWifiActiveTime(mClock.elapsedRealtime() * 1000,
                                 STATS_SINCE_CHARGED) / 1000;
                     }
                 }
